        '0.12': "Even one who writes out a single letter of it gains merit equal to building a splendid temple of Hari on the bank of the Gaṅgā, washed by her auspicious waves; here Satyatīrtha wrote out the whole commentary.",
        '0.13': "Bowing there to the Lord, out of regard for his master's word, he set out quickly with his followers; crossing many lands, the one of flawless mind reached the bank of the Godāvarī.",
        '0.14': "Scholars versed in the eighteen Vedic branches had come there to win the honours of the learned; to these examiners he expounded the Vedic passages they put forward, and he refuted the six (rival) systems.",
